      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2015 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "We aimed to assess the impact of osteoid osteomas of the hip on the size and fatty infiltration of the muscle thigh in 42 patients. The thigh circumference, cross-sectional areas, and fatty atrophy of four anterior muscles were assessed on magnetic resonance axial T1-weighted images. A significant fatty atrophy was found in the studied muscles of the ipsilateral thigh except for the rectus femoris. No significant association was demonstrated with pain duration suggesting that muscle atrophy may rather be related to the locoregional inflammation than subsequent to the disuse of the limb."
      },
